   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_step60_surface_pbl",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay_physics=1 (sfclayrev) sf_surface_physics=1 (slab) bl_pbl_physics=1 (YSU), data/eqwefic/scm_ref) dumped at the PHYSICS-DRIVER level by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (commit 592f693, module_esm_dump hooks around surface_driver + pbl_driver in dyn_em/module_first_rk_step_part1.F, dump subassembly_pbl): inputs are the phy_prep state entering surface_driver at step 60 (column its of row jps), outputs the grid fields after pbl_driver. The sfclayrev-only outputs (hfx, qfx, lh, qsfc, wspd before the slab overwrites them) come from the kernel-level dump of the same step (dumps/sfclayrev/scm_ref_120.json). All references are real32 model values, so the contract is rel 1e-5 (CLAUDE.md), widened to 2e-5 on the quantities downstream of theta_v1 - theta_vs (measured floor 4e-6, sfclayrev tests). Regime: step 60 (20:00 UTC = 13:34 LST), convective daytime land column: gsw = 315 W/m^2, slab hfx = 70.7 W/m^2 (sfclayrev's own 70.67), Ri_b = -0.044 (regime 4), u* = 0.506 m/s, h = 859 m, kpbl = 15, no cloud at the PBL top. Assertions: every surface-layer output (fluxes, u*, z0, psi functions, fm/fh, Ri_b, wind speed, 10 m wind, 2 m diagnostics, exchange coefficients, regime, theta*, 1/L) and the PBL diagnostics h, kpbl and the interface K_h/K_m columns (Linf abs 5e-3 m^2/s of a 112 m^2/s maximum, real32 dump) match pointwise. The PBL TENDENCIES are the exception and are asserted only LOOSELY: WRF's rthblten/rublten/rvblten/rqvblten are the IMPLICIT tridiagonal step's (c_new - c_old)/dt at dt = 60 s while the assembly evaluates the instantaneous right-hand side (PLAN.md 0.3: they differ by up to 41 %% of the column maximum at this step size). Measured Linf gaps at this regime: dtheta/dt 2.74e-5 K/s (rthblten max 1.81e-4, i.e. 15 %%), du/dt 5.74e-5 m/s^2 (rublten max 2.7e-4), dv/dt 1.65e-5 m/s^2, dqv/dt 2.36e-9 1/s (rqvblten max 3.9e-8); the tolerances (3.5e-5, 7.5e-5, 7.5e-5, 3e-9) sit 25-350 %% above them and document the implicit-explicit gap rather than test the physics -- the physics is pinned by the components' own small-dt tests. A stage-3 comparison at the WRF step must apply the same implicit step to the assembled tendencies. The driver-level th2/t2/q2 are overwritten by the land-surface branch of surface_driver after sfclayrev, so those three are referenced to the kernel-level sfclayrev dump.",
